  "id": "prusa-mk3s",
  "name": "Original Prusa i3 MK3S/MK3S+ extruder (E3D V6, silicone sock, MK3S+ fan shroud, SuperPINDA)",
  "provenance": "Original Prusa i3 MK3S/MK3S+ extruder (E3D V6, silicone sock, MK3S+ fan shroud, SuperPINDA) Confidence: low. Sources: https://github.com/prusa3d/Original-Prusa-i3/tree/MK3S/Printed-Parts (fan-shroud, extruder-body STEP/STL; part frames only, no assembly); https://raw.githubusercontent.com/prusa3d/Prusa-Firmware/MK3/Firmware/variants/MK3S.h (X_PROBE_OFFSET_FROM_EXTRUDER 23, Y_PROBE_OFFSET_FROM_EXTRUDER 5); https://forum.prusa3d.com/forum/original-prusa-i3-mk3s-mk3-hardware-firmware-and-software-help/super-pinda-setup (Prusa support: SuperPINDA ~1.5 mm above nozzle; old PINDA 0.8 mm); https://www.printables.com/model/57192 (SuperPINDA height tool: ~1.5 mm, 1.4-1.6 in practice); E3D V6 nozzle/heater block drawings (12.5 mm nozzle, 7 mm hex 3 mm tall, 16x20x11.5 block); PrusaSlicer MK3S profile extruder_clearance_height = 20 (nozzle tip to X rods). No assembly CAD exists in Prusa's repo for MK3S (printed parts are exported in individual part frames; the full SolidWorks assembly is Parasolid .x_b, not readable here). Geometry is assembled from published dimensions and estimates; confidence low. SuperPINDA: nominal 1.5 mm above the tip (Prusa support), set with a zip tie in the build guide (users land at 1.0-2.0); box starts at 1.1 (nominal minus 0.4 uncertainty). XY from the firmware probe offset (+23 right, +5 rear), 8 mm body + 0.5 mm. Fan shroud lowest edge estimated at 2.5 mm (sits around the sock/heater block; comparable Prusa shrouds measured 2.2-2.7: CORE One 2.2, MK4S 2.71). Its footprint is the union over the four possible orientations of the 35.3 x 27.6 mm part about the nozzle (nozzle at x -2.5 in the part frame), i.e. +/-21 mm. Heater block + sock: V6 nozzle hex 2.0-5.0, block bottom >= 5.0, sock bottom ~3.3 (1.5-1.7 mm silicone). Block footprint is the orientation union (+/-17); it lies inside the shroud footprint so orientation does not matter. X-carriage, extruder body, fan and motor boxes are coarse estimates and sit above the shroud; the slope limit is set by the shroud and the PINDA. Nozzle: land radius 0.50 mm, 48.0-degree cone to Z=2.00, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 20.00 mm above the tip, Y 18.0..36.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/prusa-mk3s.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
